{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {In order to interpret the action
 of this filter, remember that}{\ulnone 
 }{\ulnone indices increasing from zero 
toward N/2, and decreasing from N-1 toward
 N/2, represent increasingly higher frequencies}{.
 Thus, as the FIR increases in length, the
 frequency response becomes increasingly
 concentrated toward low frequencies. Thus,
 the noise, which has, on average, a broad
 band of frequencies- recall }{\ul \b Examples
 3.5}{ and }{\ul \b 3.6}{- is }{increasingly}{
 discarded. }}
}
.ATT
.STATUS Go to Section 3, p. 6
.GOTO 3_bk.mcd
