{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {We may characterize these results,
 then, in one of two equivalent ways.\par 
   }{\b 1 }{ We may observe that, as the
 FIR filter bandwidth becomes narrower, 
the rate of        fluctuation of the filter
 output decreases, or the output becomes
 smoother,               because an increasingly
 large band of frequencies of the noise 
is filtered out.\par  }{\b  2 }{ We may 
observe that, as the MA filter impulse response
 becomes longer, more        (independent)
 random variates are being averaged and 
we would expect the              output 
to tend toward the mean value sequence of
 x, which is \{1\}.}}
}
